        blocks   FAIL   blocks 59 → 60
    ACCEPTED-ROUND: "Requests to merge/split paragraphs … → rephrase inside the existing block instead." (Note for the supervisor: no other locale carries a byline in 006 at all — the clean fix is to drop the stray lt byline or to add the paragraph in the source.)
a24 — the reformat half ("1,57 mln. TWD") skipped; "TWD 1.57M" is in GUIDANCE_BIO_PRESERVED_TERMS. Only the calque was fixed.
b16 — SKIPPED (metai as plurale tantum: "1/2/3/5 metai" → "vieneri/dveji/treji/penkeri"). Grammatically right, but the checker's lt number lexicon (`SMALL_LEXICON_WORDS.lt`) only knows vienas/viena/du/dvi/trys + ordinals, so the dauginiai skaitvardžiai are not parsed and the digit disappears from the count. The sweep was applied (45 instances across 12 files) and then reverted after measuring:
